 {"q": "What is the best short definition of pietas?", "options": ["Religious feeling in private prayer", "Pity for the poor", "Dutiful loyalty to the gods, one's family and ancestors, and one's country", "Obedience to the emperor alone"], "answer": 2, "why": "Pietas covers the gods, family and country together, pictured in Aeneas carrying his father and the household gods out of Troy."},
 {"q": "Why does it matter that Jupiter's prophecy ends with a Caesar?", "options": ["It shows the poem was written before Julius Caesar lived", "It ties the gods' plan for Rome to Augustus's family, which makes the poem political", "It proves that Augustus was a god", "It shows that Virgil opposed Augustus"], "answer": 1, "why": "The Julian family claimed descent from Iülus; the gods' plan leads to the ruler of Virgil's own day."},
